      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): guard parseRequest JSON.parse against malformed WebSocket data",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Codex sandbox JSON-RPC handler parses incoming WebSocket messages with a bare JSON.parse() call without try/catch protection. A malformed or truncated WebSocket data frame causes an unhandled SyntaxError that crashes the sandbox exec server process, taking down all active sandbox sessions on that node.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe parseRequest function at extensions/codex/src/app-server/sandbox-exec-server/json-rpc.ts processes untrusted WebSocket data. Malformed JSON from network issues, client bugs, or truncated frames must be caught and handled gracefully rather than crashing the process. The fix wraps JSON.parse in try/catch and returns a structured error response.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **extensions/codex/src/app-server/sandbox-exec-server/json-rpc.ts** — wrap JSON.parse in try/catch, return JSON-RPC parse error on malformed input\n- **extensions/codex/src/app-server/sandbox-exec-server/json-rpc.test.ts** — add tests for malformed JSON, empty input, and truncated frames\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Test command\n```\nnpx vitest run extensions/codex/src/app-server/sandbox-exec-server/json-rpc.test.ts\n```\n\n### Test output\n```\n|extension-providers| ../../extensions/codex/src/app-server/sandbox-exec-server/json-rpc.test.ts (12 tests)\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  12 passed (12)\n   Duration  2.93s\n```\n\n### Behavior verification\n- Before: malformed WebSocket data → unhandled SyntaxError → sandbox process crash\n- After: malformed WebSocket data → JSON-RPC parse error response → sandbox continues serving\n\n## Related\n\nN/A (self-contained input validation improvement)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
